      "summary": ": 3 Sep 2026 Treble Cone is open, with warm spring conditions and strong, gusty weather affecting upper-mountain operations. The latest report records 3°C, winds of 32 km/h with gusts to 56 km/h, and a high freezing level. The lower mountain is expected to be soft, while warming has created wet-slide conditions in Saddle Basin, which is closed today. A front is moving up the Divide, bringing increasing cloud and changing conditions through the day. Home Basin Express and Beginner Platter are open, while Saddle Quad is closed. Home Basin is operating, but the latest 1:00 pm update says McDougall's is back open and Home Basin Lift is on wind hold, with another update due at 1:15 pm; the current lift feed therefore reflects changing wind conditions. The resort asks skiers to give others room, particularly on Lower Triple Treat where Patrol is enforcing the slow zone. (Issued: 3 Sep, 1:00 pm) Home Basin, Lowe Powder Bowl and Matukituki Basin are open; Saddle Basin, Summit Slopes and Motatapu Chutes are closed, while Backcountry and Skinning Access remain open. The access road is chain-free, though it is narrow in places and visitors should drive slowly and give way to buses.",
